tron defines a minimal time and distance along the gene in which splicing factors can be recruited. The time that it takes for pol II to reach the end of the gene defines the maximal time in which splicing could occur co-transcriptionally. Thus, the kinetics of transcription can affect the kinetics of splicing.Any covalent change in a primary (nascent) mRNA transcript is mRNA Processing.  For successful gene expression, the primary mRNA transcript needs to be converted to a mature mRNA prior to its translation into polypeptide.  Eucaryotic mRNAs undergo a series of complex processing reactions; these begin on nascent transcripts as soon as a few ribonucleotides have been synthesized during transcription by RNA Polymerase II, through the export of the mature mRNA to the cytoplasm, and culminate with mRNA turnover in the cytoplasm.","className":"Summation","schemaClass":"Summation"}],"reviewStatus":{"dbId":9821382,"displayName":"five stars","definition":"externally reviewed","name":["five stars"],"className":"ReviewStatus","schemaClass":"ReviewStatus"},"previousReviewStatus":{"dbId":9821384,"displayName":"two stars","definition":"structure updated after externally and internally reviewed","name":["two stars"],"className":"ReviewStatus","schemaClass":"ReviewStatus"},"hasDiagram":true,"hasEHLD":false,"lastUpdatedDate":"2023-03-29","hasEvent":[{"dbId":72095,"displayName":"Internal Methylation of mRNA","stId":"R-HSA-72095","stIdVersion":"R-HSA-72095.5","isInDisease":false,"isInferred":false,"maxDepth":1,"name":["Internal Methylation of mRNA"],"releaseDate":"2004-07-06","speciesName":"Homo sapiens","eventOf":[72203],"category":"transition","className":"Reaction","schemaClass":"Reaction"},{"dbId":72103,"displayName":"Formation of pre-mRNPs","stId":"R-HSA-72103","stIdVersion":"R-HSA-72103.5","isInDisease":false,"isInferred":false,"maxDepth":1,"name":["Formation of pre-mRNPs"],"releaseDate":"2004-07-06","speciesName":"Homo sapiens","eventOf":[72203],"category":"binding","clas